WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.306
DNA polymerase can proofread while copying DNA.

00:00:04.306 --> 00:00:08.403
If it adds a wrong base, its exonuclease activity removes

00:00:08.403 --> 00:00:11.211
the incorrect base from the three prime end,

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.401
allowing the correct base to be added.

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:18.348
Mismatch repair happens after replication is complete.

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:22.502
Proteins scan the new double helix for mismatched bases.

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:26.768
Specialized enzymes remove the affected section and replace it with

00:00:26.768 --> 00:00:28.859
the correct DNA nucleotides.

00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:34.992
UV light can make adjacent cytosines and thymines bond covalently,

00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:36.846
distorting the DNA.

00:00:36.846 --> 00:00:41.579
Repair proteins recognize the damage, cut out the damaged section,

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:44.922
replace the missing bases, and reseal the backbone.
